<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Increase Mather</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1639">1639</a>–<a href="/years/1723">1723</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Increase Mather was a Puritan minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a>'s North Church and president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harvard-university">Harvard College</a> from 1685 to 1701. He went to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1688 to seek the restoration of Massachusetts's charter and in 1691 obtained a new charter from William III and Mary II, which created the Province of Massachusetts Bay. He nominated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-phips">William Phips</a> as governor and wrote a cautious critique of the evidence used in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salem-witch-trials">Salem witch trials</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/increase-mather.jpg" alt="Increase Mather" width="320" height="415" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Van Veck Pinx · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Increase_Mather,_1680.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
